---
import TrustPageLayout from '@/layouts/TrustPageLayout.astro'
---

<TrustPageLayout
  title="Contact | xtarter"
  description="How to reach the xtarter project: GitHub issues for questions and bugs, SECURITY.md for responsible disclosure, and the maintainer's site."
  eyebrow="xtarter · contact"
  heading="Talk to us on GitHub."
  lede="xtarter is maintained in the open, so the fastest way to get an answer is a public thread that other users can search and learn from too."
>
  <section class="xt-section">
    <h2 class="xt-section-title">Questions, bugs, and feature ideas</h2>
    <p>
      The primary (and currently only) support channel is the project's issue tracker:{' '}
      <a
        class="xt-link"
        href="https://github.com/agustinusnathaniel/xtarter/issues"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        >github.com/agustinusnathaniel/xtarter/issues</a
      >. Open an issue for bug reports, documentation gaps, and feature requests for both CLIs,
      xtarterize and create-xtarter-app.
    </p>
    <p>
      There is no email support channel: no support inbox exists for this project, and any
      message sent privately cannot be answered. Please use the issue tracker above.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="xt-section">
    <h2 class="xt-section-title">Security reports</h2>
    <p>
      Do not report vulnerabilities in a public issue. Follow the project's responsible
      disclosure process described in{' '}
      <a
        class="xt-link"
        href="https://github.com/agustinusnathaniel/xtarter/blob/main/SECURITY.md"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        >SECURITY.md</a
      >: report privately through GitHub, include reproduction steps, and give the maintainer
      time to ship a fix before public disclosure.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="xt-section">
    <h2 class="xt-section-title">Maintainer</h2>
    <p>
      xtarter is maintained by{' '}
      <a class="xt-link" href="https://agustinusnathaniel.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer"
        >Agustinus Nathaniel</a
      >, whose personal site links current projects and writing.
    </p>
  </section>
</TrustPageLayout>
